All ten required H2 headings present, frontmatter parseable, snapshot SHA unchanged, and only the one artifact written.

**Artifact:** `docs/content-analysis/perspective-reviews/Simone-Biles/2026-08-16_020003/evidence-packet.md`

30 claims inventoried (CLM-01…CLM-30), 33 sources ledgered. Every load-bearing quote was re-verified by direct grep against the local transcripts rather than accepted from the upstream research file — the Boorman quotes, "did I do it?", "are we sure?", the two-up two-count passage, and all four Owens-backlash lines are verbatim.

**Largest unresolved evidence gap:** CLM-16 — the sentence `"It wasn't at a point of weakness, it was a point of strength."` is attributed reader-facing to the Netflix docuseries *Simone Biles Rising*, and no source located in this pass carries it. The underlying event (a therapy session the morning of the Paris all-around final, and her unease about disclosing it) is well documented, and near-variants exist from a Hoda Kotb interview — but the quoted sentence appears nowhere in `docs/content-analysis/research/Simone-Biles.md`, meaning it entered at the second-pass drafting stage with no evidence trail. The docuseries is behind an authenticated session, so it could not be audited to settle it. It sits in the section the second pass added specifically to test the article's thesis.

Three other findings evaluators would otherwise each have to rediscover, so they're stated up front in the packet:

1. **The cited podcast doesn't exist under that name.** The Boorman testimony is attributed three times reader-facing to "*Beyond Medals and Perfection* podcast." The show is **The Art of Excellence** (Glenn Zweig), Ep. 122 — "beyond medals and perfection" is episode-title text. The quotes are verbatim and the Oct 2025 date is right. The misattribution has also been committed to `scripts/blog-source-audit.mjs` OUTLETS, so the audit tool will keep grading it clean.
2. **"Nothing further" (line 440) is false as of today.** Biles disclosed a medical procedure on 22 July 2026. The *cause* is still undisclosed; the *silence* isn't — and that sentence is what the draft uses to prove its "open book about the facts, layers about the fear" reading.
3. **Both Landis left World Champions Centre in December 2024**, so "When Biles performs it, Laurent Landi stands on the landing mat" is a habitual present describing an arrangement that ended before the draft's current-tense window opens.

Two smaller quote-integrity items are logged: the draft renders "*And I think* that was my anxiety talking" as "But that was *obviously* my anxiety talking" (CLM-17), and So Syncd lists ESFJ *and* 3w2, which narrows the "three answers" framing the page's competitive claim is built on (CLM-27).

